*.sh text eol=lf
# Conformance fixtures must be byte-identical on every platform: the corpus is
# parsed by multiple language drivers, and CRLF checkouts broke the native one.
*.hsmtest text eol=lf
*.golden text eol=lf
# The Linux probe (src/probe-linux) is built and formatted only on Linux: rustfmt emits LF and
# `cargo fmt --check` fails on a CRLF checkout, and systemd parses a unit file byte-for-byte, so a
# CRLF checkout would put a stray CR at the end of every value.
*.rs text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
Cargo.lock text eol=lf
# Raw HTTP captures from the Docker Engine API (probe fixtures): the CRLF framing and chunk sizes
# ARE the test data, so git must store and check them out byte for byte.
src/probe-linux/**/fixtures/**/*.http -text
# Everything the .deb build copies into the package (maintainer scripts, copyright, the config
# skeleton) runs or is parsed on Linux: a CR would break the #!/bin/sh line of a maintainer script.
src/probe-linux/packaging/** text eol=lf
